## Session Continuity (MANDATORY at session start)

At the start of every session, BEFORE responding to anything, run these steps:

1. Check if `[MEMORY_PATH]/MEMORY.md` exists
   - If YES: read it — it is the index of all saved memories
   - If NO: create the memory directory and initialize `MEMORY.md` with an empty index header
2. Check if `[MEMORY_PATH]/work_state.md` exists
   - If YES: read it — it contains all open PRs, in-progress work, and pending items
   - If NO: create it with this blank template:
     ```markdown
     # Work State
     ## Open PRs
     ## In Progress
     ## Pending
     ```
3. Identify all items marked **PENDING** in memories and surface them at session start
4. Only after these steps: respond or act

> **How to find your MEMORY_PATH:** The path follows this exact pattern — replace `YOUR_USERNAME`
> with your Windows username (e.g., `jsmith_gusto`):
> `C:\Users\YOUR_USERNAME\.claude\projects\C--Users-YOUR_USERNAME-Documents-Projects-biztech-uipath-rpa\memory`
> If the folder does not exist yet, Claude will create it automatically on first session.

