## General Rules (apply to every session)
- Always run `git branch` before editing any file — confirm you are on a feature branch
- Fix root cause, not symptoms
- Do not add features, refactors, or abstractions beyond what the task requires
- Confirm before any destructive or irreversible action
- **Never stage or commit `CLAUDE.md` or `.claude/`** — the working `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root
  is personal config and must never be pushed. This template (`templates/CLAUDE.md.template`) is the
  exception — it lives in the skills repo and IS versioned in git.

