## Buildkite Rule — MANDATORY before any PR

Always run before push/PR:
```powershell
git fetch origin develop
git diff origin/develop..HEAD --name-only
```

If any file outside the ticket scope appears → merge develop first:
```powershell
git merge origin/develop --no-edit
git push
```

**Why this matters:** Buildkite uses `git diff origin/develop..HEAD` (two dots) to detect
which processes to validate. With two dots, any process merged into develop *after* the branch
was created appears in the diff — Buildkite then runs `check_dependency.sh` for each, failing
on processes that haven't been updated to the current lib version. Merging develop brings the
branch up to date and makes the diff show only the ticket's files.

